=== CORRECTION, appended after initial run ===
The line above reading "MISMATCH: file NOT restored correctly" was a false
alarm caused by the evidence script's own bug: the revert/restore edits to
DampedTrend.py used Python text-mode file I/O with no raw-byte backup taken
first. On this Windows Python, text-mode write silently normalizes line
endings to CRLF regardless of the file's original convention. The original
file was pure LF (0 lone LF, 0 lone CR, all via CRLF pairs after the bug).
Diagnostic: sha256(current bytes with CRLF->LF) == 57244876dc8d0711674a2fa6f4a342be68c5c2e78d100b3a0e15ffdd742fed89,
which is exactly the sha256 recorded BEFORE the revert in step 1. Confirmed
no other byte differed. Applied a binary-mode fix (CRLF->LF only, no other
translation) and re-hashed:
  sha256(TQNet/layers/DampedTrend.py) = 57244876dc8d0711674a2fa6f4a342be68c5c2e78d100b3a0e15ffdd742fed89
  MATCHES sha256 recorded before revert: True
Re-ran the phi=1 oracle test after the byte-level fix: 1 passed, 57 deselected.
Criterion 1 (sha256 before revert == sha256 after restore) is satisfied.
